.TH PENGUINTIER 1 2026-10-19 "Penguintier" "User Commands"
.\" Left-aligned, no hyphenation: command and file names stay whole.
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
penguintier \- tray app for ZeroTier networks on Linux (unofficial)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B penguintier
.RB [ \-\-autostart ]
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.br
.B penguintier \-\-version
.br
.B penguintier doctor
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B penguintier deauthorize
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B penguintier
puts your ZeroTier networks in the system tray, with the same menu as the
official ZeroTier app on macOS and Windows: your node address, joining and
leaving networks, each network's settings, status, addresses and routes,
SSO logins and saved networks.
It talks to the local ZeroTier service,
.BR zerotier\-one (8),
through its API; it does not replace it.
.PP
Penguintier also makes ZeroTier's \(lqAllow DNS Configuration\(rq work on
Linux, through
.BR systemd\-resolved (8);
see
.B DNS
below.
.PP
The icon is a StatusNotifierItem (AppIndicator).
It shows up on KDE Plasma, Xfce, Cinnamon, MATE, Budgie, LXQt, COSMIC and
bars such as waybar.
GNOME needs the \(lqAppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem Support\(rq
extension.
When no tray is found for 10 seconds, Penguintier shows one notification
with fix steps for the desktop (once per login).
.SH TRAY
Run without a command,
.B penguintier
starts the tray.
.IP \(bu 2
Started from a terminal, it starts a copy of itself in the background
(the same as
.BR "penguintier \-\-foreground" ),
with its log in the systemd journal, and returns at once.
Ctrl+C or closing the terminal does not quit it; use Quit in its menu.
.IP \(bu 2
Only one copy runs per login.
Starting it again makes the running copy show \(lqPenguintier is already running\(rq; the new one exits with status 0.
.IP \(bu 2
The first time it runs (not at login), it asks for authorization; see
.B AUTHORIZATION
below.
After the first start that reaches ZeroTier, it turns on Start at Login,
unless you changed that setting yourself.
.IP \(bu 2
It quits when the desktop session ends.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Started by the desktop at login (the Start at Login entry uses it).
Never asks for authorization by itself, and a second copy started this way
exits quietly.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Stay in the terminal, with the log on standard error, instead of moving to
the background.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage text and exit.
.PP
Options can be written with one dash or two
.RB ( \-version
is the same as
.BR \-\-version ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-\-json ]
Check everything Penguintier depends on and print one line per check:
the ZeroTier service, the API token and whether it works, the tray host,
notifications, the clipboard tools, polkit, systemd\-resolved, the DNS
daemon, each network's DNS and the state of \(lqEnable DNS
support\(rq.
Problems come with a fix, such as a command to run.
.IP
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print the report as JSON for scripts and bug reports:
.B schemaVersion
(1),
.BR ok ,
.B checks
(each with
.BR id ,
.BR title ,
.B status
.RB ( ok ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR fail
or
.BR skip ),
.BR summary ,
and optionally
.B fix
and
.BR details )
and
.BR networks .
Fields are only ever added; a change of meaning bumps
.BR schemaVersion .
The report contains your ZeroTier node address and network IDs.
.TP
.BR deauthorize " [" \-\-yes ]
Delete the token copy
.IR ~/.zeroTierOneAuthToken ,
after asking (or at once with
.BR \-\-yes ).
Penguintier and
.BR zerotier\-cli (1)
then need authorizing again.
A tray that is already running keeps working until it quits.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
ZeroTier only accepts API calls with its API token, which is in
.IR /var/lib/zerotier\-one/authtoken.secret ,
readable only by root.
On the first run, or when you click \(lqAuthorize Penguintier\&...\(rq,
Penguintier runs its token helper through
.BR pkexec (1)
(polkit action
.BR io.github.rasikhq.Penguintier.read\-token ),
which asks for your password once, and saves a copy of the token in
.I ~/.zeroTierOneAuthToken
with mode 0600.
.BR zerotier\-cli (1)
reads the same file.
.PP
Whoever has the token can fully control ZeroTier on this computer, including
joining networks and routing all traffic through one.
With the copy in your home folder, any program running as you can do that.
Penguintier refuses a token file that you don't own or that other users can
read.
.PP
Without a polkit agent (some window managers have none),
.B penguintier doctor
prints a command that makes the copy by hand.
.SH DNS
On Linux, the ZeroTier service does not apply a network's DNS settings.
The
.B penguintier\-dnsd
system service, installed with the package, does: for each network with
\(lqAllow DNS Configuration\(rq on, it tells
.BR systemd\-resolved (8)
to send queries for the network's DNS domain to the network's DNS servers,
on the network's interface only.
The domain is routing\-only (\(lq~domain\(rq) and the interface is not a
default DNS route, so other names still use your normal DNS.
It leaves alone interfaces whose DNS it did not set, and removes its
settings when the network leaves, the option is turned off, or the
service stops.
Each network's submenu has a \(lqDNS:\(rq row with the state.
.PP
On Debian without systemd\-resolved, the menu offers \(lqEnable DNS
support\&...\(rq.
It backs up
.IR /etc/resolv.conf ,
.I /etc/nsswitch.conf
and
.I /etc/systemd/resolved.conf
(if present), installs systemd\-resolved behind one password prompt, checks
that names still resolve, and undoes everything by itself when they don't.
To switch back later, run:
.PP
.RS
.B pkexec /usr/libexec/penguintier/penguintier\-dns\-helper undo
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PENGUINTIER_API_URL
Base URL of the ZeroTier API, for example
.BR http://127.0.0.1:9993 .
Overrides the port discovery (see
.BR FILES ).
Used for testing against a fake API.
.TP
.B PENGUINTIER_TOKEN_FILE
Read the API token from this file before the usual places.
.TP
.B PENGUINTIER_LIBEXEC_DIR
Look for the helper programs
.RB ( penguintier\-ui ,
.BR penguintier\-token\-helper ,
.BR penguintier\-dns\-helper )
here first, then next to the
.B penguintier
binary, then in
.IR /usr/libexec/penguintier .
.TP
.B PENGUINTIER_LOG
Log level of
.BR penguintier\-dnsd :
.BR debug ,
.B info
(default),
.B warn
or
.BR error .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings are (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zeroTierOneAuthToken
Your copy of the ZeroTier API token (mode 0600), written by
\(lqAuthorize Penguintier\&...\(rq.
The token is looked for in
.BR $PENGUINTIER_TOKEN_FILE ,
this file,
.IR ~/.zerotier\-local\-auth ,
then
.I /var/lib/zerotier\-one/authtoken.secret
(if readable).
The first file that exists is used.
.TP
.I /var/lib/zerotier\-one/zerotier\-one.port
The port of the ZeroTier API (9993 if missing).
Penguintier tries 127.0.0.1, then [::1].
.TP
.I ~/.config/penguintier/saved_networks.json
Networks you disconnected, with their settings, for Reconnect.
.TP
.I ~/.config/penguintier/state.json
What Penguintier remembers between runs (first run done, Start at Login
chosen, one\-time import done).
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.rasikhq.Penguintier.desktop
The Start at Login entry.
.TP
.I ~/.zerotier_ui/saved_networks.json
Saved networks of the official tray app, imported once.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/penguintier/no\-tray\-host\-notice
Marks that the missing\-tray notification was shown in this login.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/penguintier/
The helper programs: the Join and About windows, the token helper, the
DNS switch helper and the DNS daemon.
.TP
.I /var/lib/penguintier/dns\-backup/
The backup made by \(lqEnable DNS support\&...\(rq.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.B doctor
also exits 0 when there are only warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
.B doctor
exits 1 when a check failed;
.B deauthorize
exits 1 when nothing was deleted.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the setup, for example before reporting a bug:
.PP
.RS
.EX
penguintier doctor
penguintier doctor \-\-json > penguintier\-doctor.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch the tray's log, or run it in the terminal:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-\-user \-t penguintier \-f
penguintier \-\-foreground
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch the DNS daemon:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-u penguintier\-dnsd \-f
resolvectl status
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerotier\-cli (1),
.BR zerotier\-one (8),
.BR resolvectl (1),
.BR systemd\-resolved (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
